# Subagent-driven-development scratch: ledgers, briefs, review packages.
/.superpowers

# Comparison-harness build output. The apps live outside the workspace and
# build in place, so each one leaves artefacts next to its own sources: Gradle
# and the Kotlin compiler under bench-ktor, and a linked binary under bench-go
# that shares its name with the directory and so is not caught by any pattern
# above. The Rust apps' `target/` directories are already covered by
# `**/target` near the top of this file.
/benchmarks/bench-ktor/build
/benchmarks/bench-ktor/.kotlin
/benchmarks/bench-ktor/.gradle
/benchmarks/bench-go/bench-go
